From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c0de-coffee <53132135+c0de-coffee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:42:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hwaccel-vulkan: Only offer single-plane modifiers for
 PipeWire streams

PipeWire buffers with more than one plane are refused with "Unsupported
dma-buf: Expected exactly 1 plane for format", and the session ends.
But the modifiers offered for the stream include multi-plane ones, such
as AMD's DCC modifiers. This goes unnoticed as long as the compositor
picks a single-plane modifier; KWin picks the best one GBM allows, which
on AMD is a DCC modifier with two planes.

Only offer modifiers with one plane, like the check for BGRx support at
startup already does.
---
 src/grd-hwaccel-vulkan.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/grd-hwaccel-vulkan.c b/src/grd-hwaccel-vulkan.c
index 6f3384d..574630f 100644
--- a/src/grd-hwaccel-vulkan.c
+++ b/src/grd-hwaccel-vulkan.c
@@ -172,6 +172,8 @@ grd_hwaccel_vulkan_get_modifiers_for_format (GrdHwAccelVulkan     *hwaccel_vulka
 {
   VkPhysicalDevice vk_physical_device =
     grd_vk_physical_device_get_physical_device (physical_device);
+  /* Buffers with more planes are refused when they arrive */
+  uint32_t required_n_planes = 1;
   GArray *modifiers;
   g_autoptr (GError) error = NULL;
 
@@ -179,7 +181,8 @@ grd_hwaccel_vulkan_get_modifiers_for_format (GrdHwAccelVulkan     *hwaccel_vulka
     get_egl_vulkan_format_modifier_intersection (hwaccel_vulkan,
                                                  vk_physical_device,
                                                  drm_format,
-                                                 NULL, NULL, &error);
+                                                 &required_n_planes,
+                                                 NULL, &error);
   if (!modifiers)
     return FALSE;
 
